# Stream B candidate: rope_cache_default + AMBER (sharedgate + convinplace).
#
# Stacks the rope-cache-on toggle (which by itself should stay strict
# P37 + structured exact, see scripts/qwen36_candidate_env_rope_cache_default.env)
# on top of the existing Codex AMBER profile (sharedgate triton + linear
# attn conv triton_inplace). That AMBER profile is already known on R6000
# 2026-05-18 to:
#
#   P37 exact-greedy:           RED
#   hard structured gate:        GREEN, 40/40
#   P25 512-token decode TPS:    114.04
#   decision:                    AMBER_CANDIDATE
#
# This combined candidate exists to answer: does enabling rope cache on
# top of AMBER move the structured-40/40 P25 number above the 118 TPS
# Stream-B sprint bar without breaking structured? If yes, this is the
# new AMBER ceiling.
#
# Combined candidate status on R6000, 2026-05-18: NOT YET RUN
#   P37 exact-greedy:           pending (expected RED, inherits from AMBER)
#   hard structured gate:        pending (expected GREEN 40/40)
#   P25 512-token decode TPS:    pending (target >=118 for AMBER promote)
#   decision:                    pending
#
# Run with:
#
#   CANDIDATE_NAME=rope_cache_plus_amber \
#   CANDIDATE_ENV_FILE=scripts/qwen36_candidate_env_rope_cache_plus_amber.env \
#   scripts/r6000_qwen36_candidate_promotion_gate.sh
#
# AMBER promote thresholds (per 2026-05-18 hand-off):
#   structured 40/40 (here we still measure at the default 40/40 first;
#                     a separate hard-70/70 evaluation lives in Stream C
#                     and is opt-in for promotion to AMBER ship)
#   AND P25 512 >= 118 TPS
#   AND documented exact-greedy drift (no claim of strict P37 parity)
#
# Hard pass: 122 TPS is only available after Stream A + Stream B
# candidates each pass their own DEFAULT gate, then are combined through
# the full promotion ladder.
LYNN_FULL_ATTN_ROPE_CACHE=1
LYNN_SHARED_EXPERT_GATE_BACKEND=triton
LYNN_LINEAR_ATTN_CONV_BACKEND=triton_inplace
